# Resume-grounded interview question generator

Implement a feature to dynamically generate deterministic interview questions based on actual candidate data (projects, experiences, skills) rather than generic templates. This works offline and avoids adding a new LLM service dependency, using predefined templates populated with candidate evidence.

> [!NOTE]
> The generated questions will be added to the Candidate Details Modal inside the Admin Dashboard. A recruiter can simply click on a candidate from the search results to view their specific, resume-grounded questions.

## User Review Required

Please review the proposed deterministic templates. These will be generated locally in the UI:
1. **Experiences**: "Your resume mentions your role as **[title]** at **[firm]**. How did you validate your claimed outcomes during this time?"
2. **Abilities**: "Your resume claims: **'[ability_snippet]'**. Can you walk me through how you achieved this?"
3. **Matched Skills**: "You matched our requirement for **[skill]**. Can you describe a specific project where you applied this?"

