## Proposed Changes

### Backend Schemas
#### [MODIFY] [search.py](file:///g:/Languages/Projects/AI%20Resume%20Intelligence/backend/app/schemas/search.py)
- Update `CandidateMatch` schema to include `experiences` and `abilities` arrays. This is necessary because the search results currently only return a combined profile text and scores, missing the structured arrays for frontend templating.
- Example addition:
  ```python
  experiences: List[Dict[str, Optional[str]]] = []
  abilities: List[str] = []
  ```

---

### Backend Routes
#### [MODIFY] [search.py](file:///g:/Languages/Projects/AI%20Resume%20Intelligence/backend/app/routes/search.py)
- Update the `/candidates` search endpoint.
- When assembling the `CandidateMatch` response objects, extract and map `c.experiences` and `c.abilities` to the newly added schema fields so the frontend has access to them.

---

### Frontend Components
#### [MODIFY] [AdminDashboard.jsx](file:///g:/Languages/Projects/AI%20Resume%20Intelligence/frontend/src/pages/AdminDashboard.jsx)
- In the `expandedCandidate` modal, add a new section for "Resume-Grounded Interview Questions".
- Implement a local function to generate the list of questions based on `expandedCandidate.experiences`, `expandedCandidate.abilities`, and `expandedCandidate.score_breakdown.matched_required`.
- Render the generated questions as styled cards. Each card will show the question and a small badge or blockquote referencing the exact "evidence snippet" from the resume to fulfill the requirement that "The system does not fabricate projects or provide invented answers".

